# Website Template export (WP / Squarespace)

Canonical plan: [`docs/audit/plan-2026-08-18-website-export-wp-squarespace.md`](../../docs/audit/plan-2026-08-18-website-export-wp-squarespace.md). Lessons: [`docs/audit/session-knowledge-2026-08-18-website-export.md`](../../docs/audit/session-knowledge-2026-08-18-website-export.md).

## As-built

Single-page GitHub Pages ZIP from `generateWebsiteZip()`. Flat `WebsiteTemplateData` — no blocks, no page list, no forms (`mailto:` only). Page copy is ephemeral. Default export stays the static ZIP.

## Verdict

- **WordPress:** feasible as a **classic PHP theme ZIP** wrapping current HTML/CSS/JS (Phase 1, Medium). WXR is content-only and drops media without hosted URLs. Do not start with FSE / `theme.json` until we have a block model.
- **Squarespace 7.1:** **non-option** for theme, developer-mode, or template ZIP. No Developer Platform, no page import, no site-building API (Commerce APIs only). Do not scrape editor APIs. Do not target 7.0 Developer Mode. Do not advertise “Squarespace export.”

## Do not

- Replace GitHub Pages as the default export
- Promise a Squarespace-compatible template
- Invent a CMS/block tree solely to chase WP FSE or Squarespace Fluid Engine
